  "_about": "Post-decision regression set, added after the PR #9 review. The model was chosen on cases.json, which stays as it was when the decision was made (PLAN §8, rule 5). These cases repeat customer messages from cases.json with stricter checks, plus one new case, and are run on the chosen model only: they guard the behaviour, they do not re-open the choice. Same format and grading as cases.json. Promise exclusions are shared across the handoff cases; each case drops the ones the manual itself supports (a complaint has a 24-business-hour return time, §7.3; a customer may ask for data deletion by WhatsApp or e-mail, §9). The cases in group \"audit\" were added for issue #12 from the pre-submission audit's customer messages, with one change: \"800 reais\" became \"R$ 800\", because the grader reads only amounts written with \"R$\". They were committed before any run, and their first run is on the code before the fixes; a case that passes there is recorded as not reproduced and stays. English and Spanish cases carry the same checks as the Portuguese ones, in that language; the English order case keeps the Portuguese promise exclusions too.",
